\f1\b \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Jerusalem in previous chapters vs. Tyre's vision
\b0 \
The contrast is stark when laid out:\
Chapter 5:5 \'97 Jerusalem set 
\f3 \uc0\u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1514 \u1445 \u1493 \u1465 \u1498 \u1456 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1490 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1497 \u1460 \u1430 \u1501 
\f1  (in the midst of the nations), with lands around her. Position creates accountability.\
Chapter 16 \'97 Jerusalem as foundling made glorious, adorned with YHWH's splendor, her fame going out among nations 
\f3 \uc0\u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1497 \u1464 \u1508 \u1456 \u1497 \u1461 \u1425 \u1498 \u1456 
\f1  (through your beauty).\
Chapters 8-11 \'97 The glory that fills and departs, the sanctuary as YHWH's dwelling.\
Chapter 24:21 \'97 
\f3 \uc0\u1502 \u1463 \u1495 \u1456 \u1502 \u1463 \u1491 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1506 \u1461 \u1497 \u1504 \u1461 \u1497 \u1499 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  (the delight of your eyes), the sanctuary.\
Tyre sees: trade chokepoint. Commercial geography. Market share opened by destruction. This isn't just wrong emphasis \'97 it's categorical blindness. Tyre cannot see covenant, glory, divine dwelling, bridal relationship. Its framework has no categories for what Jerusalem 
\i was
\i0 .\

\b The ironic "more than Tyre knows"
\b0 \
This is striking. Let me trace it:\

\f3 \uc0\u1504 \u1460 \u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1512 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1491 \u1463 \u1468 \u1500 \u1456 \u1514 \u1445 \u1493 \u1465 \u1514 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1492 \u1464 \u1469 \u1506 \u1463 \u1502 \u1460 \u1468 \u1430 \u1497 \u1501 
\f1  \'97 "the door of the peoples is broken"\
But Isaiah 2:2-3: nations streaming to the mountain of YHWH's house. The peoples coming. And here \'97 the door is broken open. What Tyre sees as removed barrier to trade might describe removed exclusivity. The gate that controlled access is... opened?\

\f3 \uc0\u1504 \u1464 \u1505 \u1461 \u1443 \u1489 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1488 \u1461 \u1500 \u1464 \u1425 \u1497 
\f1  \'97 "it has turned to me"\
Tyre means trade redirects. But turning (
\f3 \uc0\u1513 \u1473 \u1493 \u1468 \u1489 
\f1  and related forms) carries covenant weight throughout Ezekiel \'97 turning away, turning back. The peoples turning... somewhere.\

\f3 \uc0\u1488 \u1460 \u1502 \u1464 \u1468 \u1469 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1430 \u1492 
\f1  \'97 "I will be filled"\
This is temple language. The glory fills (
\f3 \uc0\u1502 \u1464 \u1500 \u1461 \u1488 
\f1 ). Tyre expects to be filled with commerce. But the filling of the temple was glory. And that glory departed. And will return. Who gets filled through this broken gate?\

\f3 \uc0\u1492 \u1464 \u1469 \u1495 \u1459 \u1512 \u1464 \u1469 \u1489 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  \'97 "she is laid waste"\
The explanation, for Tyre, of why the above occurs. But 
\f3 \uc0\u1495 \u1464 \u1512 \u1456 \u1489 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  connects to sword and destruction throughout Ezekiel. The devastation that creates... what?\
Tyre's commercial summary might accidentally prophesy: the exclusive door broken, peoples turning, someone being filled \'97 through Jerusalem's destruction.\

\b The recognition formula and chapter 25
\b0 \
The previous instance noted that chapter 25 contained the first positive covenant language after twenty-four chapters of condemnation \'97 
\f3 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1502 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1497 \u1460 \u1513 \u1456 \u1474 \u1512 \u1464 \u1488 \u1461 \u1500 
\f1  (MY people Israel) in 25:14. YHWH's fury at those who gloated revealed continuing relationship.\
Now in 26:6: 
\f3 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1497 \u1464 \u1469 \u1491 \u1456 \u1506 \u1430 \u1493 \u1468 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1499 \u1460 \u1468 \u1469 \u1497 \u1470 \u1488 \u1458 \u1504 \u1460 \u1445 \u1497 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1497 \u1456 \u1492 \u1465 \u1493 \u1464 \u1469 \u1492 
\f1  \'97 the daughters in the field will know. But this formula has shifted context. In chapters 1-24, Israel's recognition often comes through judgment on themselves. In chapters 25-32, nations recognize through their own judgment.\
Yet the recognition is the same: 
\f3 \uc0\u1488 \u1458 \u1504 \u1460 \u1445 \u1497 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1497 \u1456 \u1492 \u1465 \u1493 \u1464 \u1469 \u1492 
\f1 . The one who judges Israel is the one who judges those who gloat over that judgment. Universal sovereignty becomes visible through both movements.\

\b Forward in chapter 26
\b0 \
Verses 7-14 shift from "many nations" (
\f3 \uc0\u1490 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1497 \u1460 \u1443 \u1501 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1512 \u1463 \u1489 \u1460 \u1468 \u1428 \u1497 \u1501 
\f1 ) to specifically Nebuchadnezzar \'97 
\f3 \uc0\u1502 \u1462 \u1443 \u1500 \u1462 \u1498 \u1456 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1502 \u1456 \u1500 \u1464 \u1499 \u1460 \u1425 \u1497 \u1501 
\f1  (king of kings). The wave imagery suggests repeated assaults, which the specific naming then begins. But the specificity after generality creates interpretive space \'97 is Nebuchadnezzar one wave among many? The historical Nebuchadnezzar besieged Tyre for thirteen years without fully taking the island. Alexander later succeeded. Does the text know something about extended fulfillment?\
Verse 5: 
\f3 \uc0\u1502 \u1460 \u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1496 \u1463 \u1448 \u1495 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1495 \u1458 \u1512 \u1464 \u1502 \u1460 \u1434 \u1497 \u1501 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1469 \u1492 \u1456 \u1497 \u1462 \u1492 \u1433 
\f1  \'97 "you will become a spreading place for nets." The great commercial power reduced to bare utility for fishermen. The inversion is precise: Tyre's ships become... rocks where poor laborers dry nets.\
<notes>The dating puzzle remains genuinely puzzling. The eleventh year places this during or just after Jerusalem's fall. The missing month might indicate the timing is the point \'97 whenever during the eleventh year this was spoken, Tyre had already said 
\f3 \uc0\u1492 \u1462 \u1488 \u1464 \u1495 
\f1 . Or perhaps the ambiguity makes the oracle applicable across the extended siege period. But I'm not confident.</notes>\
What do you see in the rest of the chapter that might further illuminate verses 1-6?
\f0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
