Having done that may assist in addressing the difficulties in verses 19-21.\'a0 Why bring up the deep, as in the waters when the LORD made the world but it was still formless and void, or the flood in the days of Noah?\'a0 Is the grave literal, of the people, or figurative, of the nation?\'a0 Why bring up the eternal nature of going down to the pit; are there reasons or textures beyond the irreversible nature of the LORD's judgement?\'a0 How is the eternal nature of going down to the pit linked to the terror which wraps up and connects sections of judgement on Tyre in chapters 26, 27, and 28?\'a0 Is the horror of verse 21 an objective state of Tyre, or a perception by witnesses?
