\b0 \
You're right to press this. I was unclear because I was conflating different sources.\
The previous instance's message about chapter 25 focused on: possessive pronouns persisting through judgment (MY sanctuary, MY people, MY vengeance), vengeance presupposing relationship, and the first positive covenant language after twenty-four chapters of condemnation.\
The Sheol material \'97 nations bearing shame despite powerlessness \'97 appears in the message about chapters 4-5, referencing chapter 37's background, not chapter 25 directly.\
What I should have said: Chapter 26:20's descent to the pit with 
\f3 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1501 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1506 \u1493 \u1465 \u1500 \u1464 \u1501 
